      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "HTTP::Session versions before 0.54 for Perl allow memcached command injection via unfiltered session ids in HTTP::Session::Store::CHI.\n\nThe session id from the client's cookie reaches the CHI cache unchanged. The sibling HTTP::Session::Store::Memcached rejects ids that contain control characters, but the CHI store has no such check, and CHI does not escape keys for its memcached drivers.\n\nWith a memcached driver, a CR and LF in the session id end the cache command early, and the server reads the bytes after them as further commands.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
